{%- comment -%}
  Sitewide scrub of specific-timing claims ("asleep in 10–15 minutes", "works in
  minutes", "from the first night"…). Meta flags timed sleep claims, and much of this
  copy lives in template JSON, settings_data, metafields and SEO descriptions that a
  git deploy can't reliably change, so layout/theme.liquid pipes the finished page
  through here. Usage directions ("15–20 minutes before bed") and competitor
  digestion times are intentionally left alone.
  Reviews that state a timing are skipped in the review sections themselves
  (customer-testimonials-video, real-stories-v2, story-reviews-v2, page-cta-v2).
{%- endcomment -%}
